      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That \"scurrying\" feeling you're describing is the result of the specific frequency distribution of the turbulent energy, which is what linguists call the noise spectrum. Instead of a single, uniform rush, the friction generates a broad range of high-frequency energy—the hiss or buzz—because the air molecules are colliding chaotically against the narrow constriction. Imagine a swarm of tiny, high-pitched, disorganized little sounds all happening at once, which is exactly what a proper, well-formed fricative requires.",
